libcamera: sensor: Add imx471 sensor delays

The imx471 entry has no sensor delays, so libcamera assumes exposure 2,
gain 1. Measured on the ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 14 by stepping each control
alone with AE off and timing the change in brightness against the frame at
whose start DelayedControls wrote it: both exposure and analogue gain take
effect 2 frames later. With gain assumed at 1, AGC pairs each frame's
statistics with the wrong gain and oscillates at startup. The blanking
delays are libcamera's defaults, not measured.

--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -310,7 +310,12 @@
 				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeColorBarsFadeToGray, 3 },
 				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModePn9, 4 },
 			},
-			.sensorDelays = { },
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
 		} },
 		{ "imx477", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 1550, 1550 },
